wer Silesia, south-western Poland, at the foot of the Table Mountains near the Czech border.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/kudungga"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kudungga.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Kudungga</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Kudungga is the earliest known ruler of Kutai in eastern Borneo, named in the Sanskrit yupa inscriptions of his grandson Mulavarman from around 400.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/kudur-mabuk"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kudur-mabuk.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Kudur-Mabuk</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Kudur-Mabuk was an Amorite chief of the Yamutbal tribe in the region east of the Tigris, whose name is Elamite.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/kue-na"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kue-na.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Kue Na</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Kue Na was a king of Lan Na from 1355 to 1385, remembered as a pious and learned ruler.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/kuelap"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kuelap.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Kuélap</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Kuélap is a walled settlement of the Chachapoya culture on a ridge above the Utcubamba valley in Amazonas, northern Peru, built mainly from about the 6th century CE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/kufa"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kufa.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Kufa</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Kufa was a garrison city founded by Arab Muslim forces in southern Iraq in the 630s during the Rashidun conquests.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/kufra"><span class="enc-name">Kufra</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Kufra is a group of oases in the Libyan Desert of south-eastern Libya.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/kuito"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kuito.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Kuito</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Kuito is the capital of Bié Province in the central highlands of Angola.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/kujula-kadphises"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kujula-kadphises.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Kujula Kadphises</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Kujula Kadphises was the founder of the Kushan Empire in the 1st century CE.</span></a></li></ul>
